          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: In 2005 (the witness does not remember the exact date) around 10 PM, a student was about to close his Velux window when he was surprised to see a bright object pass at great speed across the clear sky. Its trajectory is from North-West to South-East. With a spherical shape and slightly yellowish hue, this object appears to be at an altitude of 3000 meters, no noise is heard. It seems caught in a halo. The observation lasts less than 3 seconds. The description of the object could suggest a probable atmospheric reentry, but we lack information about the observed phenomenon.",
